         appearance: (color: "#d6cebb", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "The hardest of the temperate woods ('ironwood'): mallets, cogs, and excellent fuel."),
            (id: "larch_wood", name: "larch", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "softwood", "resinous", "construction", "durable"], density_kg_m3: 590,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 52, bending_mpa: 92), elastic_modulus_gpa: 12.5,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 280), fuel_mj_kg: 19.0, workability: 0.65, durability: 0.6,
         appearance: (color: "#d9a877", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "The heaviest and most lasting of the conifers: posts, sills and boats; its heartwood stands the wet."),
        (id: "fir_wood", name: "fir", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "softwood", "construction"], density_kg_m3: 410,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 34, bending_mpa: 61), elastic_modulus_gpa: 9.5,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 280), fuel_mj_kg: 18.0, workability: 0.85, durability: 0.1,
         appearance: (color: "#d9cdb4", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Light, straight and soft; rots quickly in the open; its blisters hold a clear balsam."),
        (id: "mesquite_wood", name: "mesquite", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "hardwood", "durable"], density_kg_m3: 800,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 60, bending_mpa: 110), elastic_modulus_gpa: 11.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 300), fuel_mj_kg: 19.5, workability: 0.4, durability: 0.8,
         appearance: (color: "#8a4a2a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Hard, heavy and stable: it burns long and hot to a bed of coals, and its posts outlast those of any other desert wood."),
        (id: "saxaul_wood", name: "saxaul", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "hardwood"], density_kg_m3: 1050,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 70, bending_mpa: 100), elastic_modulus_gpa: 12.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 310), fuel_mj_kg: 19.0, workability: 0.2, durability: 0.7,
         appearance: (color: "#7a6a5a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.6),
         notes: "So dense it sinks, brittle and twisted: no timber, but the best fuel of the Central Asian deserts, burning almost like coal."),
        (id: "tamarisk_wood", name: "tamarisk", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "hardwood"], density_kg_m3: 700,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 45, bending_mpa: 80), elastic_modulus_gpa: 9.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 290), fuel_mj_kg: 18.0, workability: 0.6, durability: 0.5,
         appearance: (color: "#c89a7a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Pinkish, close-grained and smooth: tool handles, small carvings and the desert's firewood."),
        (id: "acacia_wood", name: "acacia", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "hardwood"], density_kg_m3: 850,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 55, bending_mpa: 100), elastic_modulus_gpa: 11.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 300), fuel_mj_kg: 19.0, workability: 0.4, durability: 0.6,
         appearance: (color: "#a8703a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Hard and heavy, red-brown at the heart: the savanna's firewood, its posts and its tool handles."),
        (id: "baobab_wood", name: "baobab wood", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood"], density_kg_m3: 230,
         fracture: Fibrous, strength: (compressive_mpa: 8, bending_mpa: 15), elastic_modulus_gpa: 1.5,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 260), fuel_mj_kg: 12.0, workability: 0.9, durability: 0.05,
         appearance: (color: "#e0d0b0", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.8),
         notes: "Spongy and full of water, it holds no fire and no shape: the baobab is worth its fruit, its leaves and its bark, not its wood."),
        (id: "marula_wood", name: "marula", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood", "carving"], density_kg_m3: 560,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 35, bending_mpa: 70), elastic_modulus_gpa: 8.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 280), fuel_mj_kg: 17.5, workability: 0.8, durability: 0.2,
         appearance: (color: "#d8c8a8", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Pale and even: bowls, mortars, spoons and drums."),
        (id: "mopane_wood", name: "mopane", category: Wood, tags: ["firewood", "hardwood", "durable"], density_kg_m3: 1100,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 80, bending_mpa: 130), elastic_modulus_gpa: 15.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 320), fuel_mj_kg: 20.0, workability: 0.2, durability: 0.9,
         appearance: (color: "#664231", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.4),
         notes: "One of the heaviest woods there is, dark and oily: the termites leave its posts alone, and it burns long and hot."),
        (id: "teak_wood", name: "teak", category: Wood, tags: ["hardwood", "construction", "durable"], density_kg_m3: 650,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 58, bending_mpa: 100), elastic_modulus_gpa: 12.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 300), fuel_mj_kg: 18.5, workability: 0.7, durability: 0.95,
         appearance: (color: "#b08a5a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.4),
         notes: "Golden-brown and oily, it neither warps nor rots, and shrugs off shipworm and termite: the boatbuilder's wood."),
        (id: "mahogany_wood", name: "mahogany", category: Wood, tags: ["hardwood", "construction"], density_kg_m3: 550,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 45, bending_mpa: 80), elastic_modulus_gpa: 10.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 300), fuel_mj_kg: 18.0, workability: 0.8, durability: 0.6,
         appearance: (color: "#8a3a2a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.4),
         notes: "Red-brown, straight-grained and stable: canoes hollowed from one trunk, and furniture."),
        (id: "kapok_wood", name: "kapok wood", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood"], density_kg_m3: 300,
         fracture: Fibrous, strength: (compressive_mpa: 15, bending_mpa: 30), elastic_modulus_gpa: 3.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 260), fuel_mj_kg: 15.0, workability: 0.9, durability: 0.05,
         appearance: (color: "#d9ceb3", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.7),
         notes: "Light and soft: dugout canoes that float even swamped, and little else."),
        (id: "fig_wood", name: "fig wood", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood"], density_kg_m3: 450,
         fracture: Fibrous, strength: (compressive_mpa: 25, bending_mpa: 45), elastic_modulus_gpa: 6.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 270), fuel_mj_kg: 16.0, workability: 0.8, durability: 0.1,
         appearance: (color: "#d8ccb0", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.6),
         notes: "Pale, soft and quick to rot; fire drills are spun from it and its inner bark is beaten into cloth."),
        (id: "palm_wood", name: "palm wood", category: Wood, tags: ["construction"], density_kg_m3: 600,
         fracture: Fibrous, strength: (compressive_mpa: 30, bending_mpa: 60), elastic_modulus_gpa: 7.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 280), fuel_mj_kg: 16.5, workability: 0.5, durability: 0.4,
         appearance: (color: "#8a6a4a", color2: "#3a2a1a", pattern: Fibrous, roughness: 0.8),
         notes: "Not wood at all but bundles of hard fibres in pith: a palm trunk splits along its length into beams, posts and rafters."),
        (id: "brazil_nut_wood", name: "Brazil nut wood", category: Wood, tags: ["hardwood", "construction"], density_kg_m3: 750,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 55, bending_mpa: 100), elastic_modulus_gpa: 13.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 300), fuel_mj_kg: 18.5, workability: 0.6, durability: 0.6,
         appearance: (color: "#a8805a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Strong and straight-grained, from the trunk of a giant."),
        (id: "rubber_wood", name: "rubber wood", category: Wood, tags: ["hardwood"], density_kg_m3: 600,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 35, bending_mpa: 65), elastic_modulus_gpa: 9.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 290), fuel_mj_kg: 17.0, workability: 0.8, durability: 0.2,
         appearance: (color: "#e0d0b0", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Pale and even, but it rots and is eaten by beetles soon after it is cut."),
        (id: "cacao_wood", name: "cacao wood", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood"], density_kg_m3: 500,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 25, bending_mpa: 45), elastic_modulus_gpa: 6.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 280), fuel_mj_kg: 16.0, workability: 0.8, durability: 0.1,
         appearance: (color: "#c8b090", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.6),
         notes: "A small tree's soft wood: kindling and stakes."),
        (id: "meranti_wood", name: "meranti", category: Wood, tags: ["hardwood", "construction"], density_kg_m3: 550,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 42, bending_mpa: 75), elastic_modulus_gpa: 10.5,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 290), fuel_mj_kg: 18.0, workability: 0.8, durability: 0.4,
         appearance: (color: "#b06a4a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Pinkish-red and coarse, in long clear lengths from the dipterocarps' tall stems."),
        (id: "durian_wood", name: "durian wood", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood"], density_kg_m3: 550,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 35, bending_mpa: 60), elastic_modulus_gpa: 8.5,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 285), fuel_mj_kg: 17.0, workability: 0.7, durability: 0.2,
         appearance: (color: "#c89a7a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.6),
         notes: "Reddish and plain: posts and planks that do not last in the wet."),
        (id: "bamboo", name: "bamboo", category: Wood, tags: ["construction", "container", "pole"], density_kg_m3: 700,
         fracture: Fibrous, strength: (compressive_mpa: 60, bending_mpa: 140, tensile_mpa: 200), elastic_modulus_gpa: 17.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 280), fuel_mj_kg: 17.0, workability: 0.7, durability: 0.4,
         appearance: (color: "#c8b060", color2: "#6a7a3a", pattern: Banded, roughness: 0.3),
         notes: "Hollow, jointed culms as strong for their weight as steel: split for weaving, whole for posts, pipes, rafts and cooking vessels, sharpened for knives and spearheads."),
        (id: "banana_stem", name: "banana stem", category: PlantTissue, tags: ["fibre", "natural"], density_kg_m3: 400,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 260), fuel_mj_kg: 5.0, workability: 0.9, durability: 0.05,
         appearance: (color: "#c8d0a0", pattern: Layered, roughness: 0.5),
         notes: "Not wood: sheath upon sheath of soft leaf base, full of water and long fibres."),
        (id: "cedar_wood", name: "cedar", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood", "construction", "carving", "aromatic", "firewood"], density_kg_m3: 560,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 45, bending_mpa: 80), elastic_modulus_gpa: 9.0,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 290), fuel_mj_kg: 19.0, workability: 0.85, durability: 0.9,
         appearance: (color: "#c88a5a", pattern: WoodGrain, roughness: 0.4),
         notes: "Fragrant, reddish and rot-proof: the wood of temples, bridges and chests that keep moths from wool."),
        (id: "cypress_wood", name: "cypress", category: Wood, tags: ["softwood", "construction", "boat", "firewood"], density_kg_m3: 510,
         fracture: Splintery, strength: (compressive_mpa: 43, bending_mpa: 73), elastic_modulus_gpa: 9.9,
         thermal: (ignition_c: 290), fuel_mj_kg: 19.0, workability: 0.85, durability: 0.95,
